From 668ba692ade59c350bac9216d5bc785d01754054 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 00:14:15 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ship oniguruma's licence alongside onigurumacffi's own

The extension dynamically links the oniguruma C library, built from
source and installed by our riscv64 CI before compiling the cffi
extension; auditwheel then vendors the resulting libonig.so into the
wheel (onigurumacffi.libs/), same as every platform wheel published to
PyPI. Oniguruma is BSD-2-Clause and its binary-redistribution clause
requires the copyright notice to travel with the binary, but
setup.cfg's explicit license_files list names only onigurumacffi's own
LICENSE, so the built wheel ships a single notice covering the wrapper
alone.

license_files is an explicit list (gotcha 57: it replaces setuptools'
default LICEN[CS]E*/COPYING*/NOTICE*/AUTHORS* glob rather than adding
to it), so the fix has to extend the list, not just drop a file next
to it. Our CI stages oniguruma's own COPYING as LICENSE.oniguruma at
the project root before the build.

Upstream-Status: To upstream [not yet submitted; the same gap exists in every onigurumacffi wheel on PyPI, so this needs a maintainer discussion rather than a drive-by PR]

Signed-off-by: Ludovic Henry <git@ludovic.dev>
---
 setup.cfg | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/setup.cfg b/setup.cfg
index e9eb50a..5cef1d6 100644
--- a/setup.cfg
+++ b/setup.cfg
@@ -8,7 +8,9 @@ url = https://github.com/asottile/onigurumacffi
 author = Anthony Sottile
 author_email = asottile@umich.edu
 license = MIT
-license_files = LICENSE
+license_files =
+    LICENSE
+    LICENSE.oniguruma
 classifiers =
     Programming Language :: Python :: 3
     Programming Language :: Python :: 3 :: Only
-- 
